126 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (The UTS Cyber Security Society \(CSEC\) is a not-for-profit student-run initiative at the University of Technology Sydney. Our team is dedicated to bridging the gap between academia and industry by arming students with the practical skills necessary to launch their careers in information security. CSEC is one of the largest IT society at UTS with over 900 financial members in 2025.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
127 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (At CSEC, we aim to be the leading hub of cyber security education. As a professional development society, we strive to provide high calibre and quality education for our members. Furthermore, we seek to leave our members with multifaceted skills that they can still apply after university. We acknowledge the importance of catering to all skill levels, knowing that we all started our journey as beginners. This in turn creates an environment where all members are made to feel welcome, enabling us to promote cyber security culture and awareness. Being a people-centric, not for profit organisation, we offer ongoing support, career mindfulness, and eagerness to foster the security community.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
128 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (We strive to make an impactful difference, not only for our members but the wider community. This can clearly be seen through our outreach engagements with high school students and those already in the industry. Within our member base we focus on not only educating, but empowering all individuals through events such as CSECcon.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
129 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (Our team is comprised of many passionate individuals with a variety of strengths and talents. Particularly notable, we have our talented Advisory Board on our team who have graduated and are currently employed, skilled cyber security professionals. Thus, CSEC has the advantage of hearing the perspectives of those in industry, knowing the trends, and ensuring our content remains relevant.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
